<title>SINGAPORE: Marco Polo net profit up 12.94 pct.</title>
<headline>Marco Polo net profit up 12.94 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		18.27	vs     16.18</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	   4.00	vs	3.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	4.58	vs	4.06</p>
<p>    Turnover		  77.22	vs    151.98</p>
<p>    Other income	     2.61	vs	1.12</p>
<p>    Interest expense	 9.49	vs     10.56</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     5.00	vs	6.37</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  22.91	vs     23.77</p>
<p>    Associates		(0.14)     vs     (0.007)</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.50	vs	7.59</p>
<p>Dividend pay/register - August 29 1997 / August 19 1997 </p>
<p>Note - Hotel and property company Marco Polo Developments Ltd said turnover fell 49 percent due mainly to lower revenue resulting from the completion of its Parc Oasis development. The increase in net profit was attributable to lower than expected cost of the Parc Oasis development, improved rental income and the write-back of over-provision for property tax on Wheelock Place.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
